{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"46246623-c89e-47ae-919a-2eefef0ff011","runId":"f8399a50-bd9a-4d40-b21d-948f4b075ae1","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":20,"previousEventHash":"sha256:bb062aa60a1748e58a52bf1c2f4a3c7f0e478fa9bc6833a5611c64159a3345a4","type":"phase.completed","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a04358-c969-7a5a-9b8c-48fd23aadf57","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-27T13:17:57.335Z","idempotencyKey":"phase:plan:1:complete","payload":{"phase":"plan","attempt":1,"evidence":[],"report":"<!-- FORGE:CONTRACT -->\n## Builder Contract\n\n### Objective\n\nLock in the existing `setWorkflowLabel` positive safe-integer boundary with focused regression coverage proving malformed runtime issue numbers are rejected before any GitHub transport request.\n\n### Allowed Paths\n\n- `test/adapters/github-projection.test.ts`\n\n### Forbidden Changes\n\n- Do not change production projector behavior or GitHub API routes.\n- Do not change workflow policy, schemas, labels, comments, or artifact formats.\n- Do not modify verification commands or dependency metadata.\n- Do not broaden coverage beyond the issue-number validation regression.\n\n### Invariants\n\n- Invalid issue numbers fail with `TypeError` and the established message `Issue number must be positive.`\n- Validation occurs before any transport request or API path construction.\n- Existing valid workflow-label transitions remain unchanged.\n- The patch stays test-only unless fresh evidence disproves the frozen-base investigation.\n\n### Deliverables\n\n- A focused adapter regression test covering representative unsafe runtime values.\n- Evidence that the transport is not called for rejected values.\n- A passing required `check` verification.\n- Fresh correctness and security review of the exact committed head.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] **AC-1:** Validate the report against the frozen base.\n- [x] **AC-2:** Preserve the already-correct production guard.\n- [ ] **AC-3:** Add focused malformed-input/no-transport regression coverage.\n- [ ] **AC-4:** Pass required local verification and fresh exact-head review.\n\n<!-- FORGE:CONTEXT -->\n## Implementation Context\n\n### History\n\nIssue #209 carries security finding `security-001` from PR #199. The frozen `staging` base already contains both the public `setWorkflowLabel` check and the shared `#replaceWorkflowLabel` check, making the original finding stale at this head.\n\n### Callers And Data Flow\n\n`setWorkflowLabel(issueNumber, workflowLabel, signal)` validates its arguments, then delegates to `#replaceWorkflowLabel`. That private method validates `issueNumber` before constructing issue and label routes and before invoking `GitHubTransport.request`.\n\n### CI Surface\n\nThe tracked required check is `npm run check`, which runs TypeScript type checking and the complete Node test suite. Authoritative GitHub CI remains parent-owned after PR creation.\n\n### Prior Findings\n\nThe only supplied finding is the stale medium-severity security report that malformed runtime values could enter GitHub paths. The test must directly prove the relevant fail-closed boundary.\n\n### Hazards\n\n- TypeScript annotations alone do not protect JavaScript or deserialized runtime callers.\n- A weak test that only checks rejection but not transport silence could miss validation occurring after a request.\n- Broad production refactoring would add risk without fixing a reproducible defect.\n\n<!-- FORGE:CONTEXT:COMPLETE -->\n\n<!-- FORGE:ARCHITECT -->\n## Implementation Plan\n\n1. Add one focused test in `test/adapters/github-projection.test.ts` using a transport that fails if called.\n2. Exercise representative malformed runtime values, including path-like strings cast across the TypeScript boundary and invalid numeric values.\n3. Assert the established `TypeError` message for each value and assert zero transport calls.\n4. Run the required bound `check`, commit the implementation, prepare the PR, and launch the required fresh reviewer panel at the frozen head.\n\n<!-- FORGE:ARCHITECT:COMPLETE -->"}}
